scaleplex: vf_inlineass AMD-Vulkan branch — sub-burn via libplacebo pl_render_image (#123)

AMD-Vulkan hardware branch for vf_inlineass, mirroring the Intel iHD
VAAPI-VPP branch (patch 0115) and the NVIDIA CUDA branch (patch 0126) in
purpose: GPU-resident text/ASS + bitmap (PGS/DVD/DVB) burn-in onto VAAPI
surfaces, no per-frame hwdownload.

Why a separate branch on AMD radeonsi:
  - overlay_vaapi + tonemap_vaapi are Intel-iHD-only (radeonsi has no
    VPP blend pipeline), so the existing patch-0115 path cannot run.
  - overlay_vulkan on RADV crashes with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST + amdgpu
    GPU reset (driver bug, kernel-side).
  - libplacebo's `inputs=2` (multi-input filter mode) hits the libplacebo
    Vulkan assert `vk_tex_barrier: !tex_vk->held`.
  Both fail at the driver/library plumbing level. The recipe-tuning
  effort on Mesa 25.2.8 / RADV NAVI21 / RX 6800 explored 14 graph shapes;
  none worked at production quality.

What works: mpv vo_gpu_next's update_overlays() uses libplacebo's
pl_render_image() + pl_overlay API directly. pl_render_image dispatches
via libplacebo's own draw_overlays() — a different libplacebo code path
than the broken inputs=2 front-door. mpv ships this on AMD RADV in
production today. This patch ports that blueprint into vf_inlineass.

Architecture:
  - At config_input time on AV_PIX_FMT_VAAPI, vaQueryVendorString()
    selects the branch: "Mesa" substring → AMD-Vulkan (this patch);
    otherwise → existing VAAPI-VPP branch.
  - inlineass_amd_vk_config() derives a Vulkan AVHWDeviceContext from
    the input VAAPI device via the DRM intermediary (direct VAAPI→Vulkan
    derive is broken on jellyfin-ffmpeg7 — the same recipe-tuning
    finding that ruled out overlay_vulkan), then imports that device
    into libplacebo. The pl_vulkan_import_params queue family + lock/
    unlock bridging is cribbed verbatim from vf_libplacebo.c init_vulkan().
  - Per-frame: libass renders the band into the shared `cpu` BGRA staging
    (same buffer the VAAPI-VPP branch uses); uploaded to a cached
    pl_tex; the source + a freshly-allocated output VAAPI surface (from
    the input frames pool) are mapped as pl_frame via pl_map_avframe_ex
    (libplacebo handles VAAPI→DMA-BUF→Vulkan transparently); the band is
    attached as a pl_overlay; pl_render_image() blends + writes the
    output surface. Output stays AV_PIX_FMT_VAAPI for the downstream
    h264/hevc_vaapi encoder.
  - Bitmap (PGS) reuses the existing bmp_pending_buf premultiplied BGRA
    staging populated by avfilter_inlineass_replay_bitmap; uploaded to a
    separate cached pl_tex.

Gated on CONFIG_LIBPLACEBO_FILTER (the same guard vf_libplacebo uses).
The scaleplex deps image is built with --enable-libplacebo --enable-vulkan
since the 0094 lineage, so the guard is true for every shipped
scaleplex-ffmpeg build. A libplacebo-less ffmpeg sees neither the
includes nor the branch — the existing VAAPI-VPP / CUDA / SW paths are
untouched.

Tracks issue #123 (AMD RX 6800 radeonsi bring-up).
